# Live UI preview

The agent handles code. Devo handles the human UI himself and reiterates it. Do not restyle UI he will fix.

Any UI change that is not yet what he should look at needs a clickable live preview he can open. Screenshots are not enough.

- Before it is on the public host: run the real Next server (`npm run dev`, port 43181) and put the Cursor preview link (or cloudflared tunnel) at the top of the PR description and in a PR comment.
- Once the public host is the thing to look at: [https://humanehealth.devoutshaman.com](https://humanehealth.devoutshaman.com).
- He walks `/` and the five desks: `/ops/wellness`, `/ops/diagnostic`, `/ops/unnaturalfertility`, `/ops/cosmetic`, `/ops/stimulants`.
- Code publishes through GitHub to `main`, then that host. Cloud Run `humanehealth-web`, project `devo-holding`, region `us-west1`. DNS is already a CNAME to `ghs.googlehosted.com`. Do not change Cloudflare. Do not add DNS. No throwaway host. No new pull request unless a real code change needs one.
